STEP 1 — Project folders and .gitignore

What I did:
- Created the main project folders:
    backend/   -> the Python/FastAPI side
    frontend/  -> the React (Vite) side
    docs/      -> these step-by-step notes
    test/      -> small test scripts (nothing else goes here)
- Also created the backend package folders:
    backend/app/
    backend/app/core/   (settings)
    backend/app/db/      (database)
- Updated the existing .gitignore. It already ignored Python stuff, .env,
  venv/ and build output. I added a Node section so Git ignores:
    node_modules/        (huge, re-installable)
    frontend/dist/, frontend/build/   (frontend build output)
    .vite/ and npm/yarn/pnpm debug logs

Why:
- Clean separation between backend and frontend from day one.
- Git should never track installed dependencies or secret files.
